% over 6 months and 29% over 1 year.\n- Implied sits about 5–7 vol points below realized. If realized vol persists, the calls look cheap.\n- Realized vol could fall back, so the gap is not a guaranteed edge.\n\n**CMA policy path**\n- The CMA held at 4.50% in October 2026. Governor Ashby's base case is one 25bp cut in 2027.\n- Futures price about 50bp of cuts by the end of 2027, so the market is about 25bp more dovish than the CMA.\n- A repricing toward the CMA's path would cut the P/E on VLTX's long-duration grid-equipment basket by roughly 0.75 points, about 4% of 19x. That figure is a rough linear extrapolation of the factsheet's 1.5 points per 50bp.\n- Long-dated calls would feel this through both rho and the forward.\n- Ashby's comments make a hawkish repricing the more likely direction, so I expect a modestly negative effect, with event risk around CMA meetings.\n\n**Gaps**\n- I found no VLTX spot, strike, premium, rate or dividend data. I couldn't compute option prices, break-evens or a model value, so \"attractively priced\" rests on implied versus realized vol alone.\n- I haven't checked whether VLTX's current price already reflects the CMA's stance.\n\n**Takeaway:** The cheap vol is a reasonable case for owning the calls. A roughly 4% valuation headwind from hawkish repricing partly offsets it. To size or time a trade, you'd need the actual quotes.\n\nDetail is in n4.r1 (policy path) and n5.r1 (volatility).","ttft_ms":4236,"type":"result","duration_ms":52405,"uuid":"da2179e4-642d-40d5-a3ad-dd4de1f04a88","ttft_stream_ms":2984,"time_to_request_ms":126,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":10,"system_prompt":5,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":5,"input_attachments":14,"input_hooks":6,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":3,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":9,"init_frame_send":7,"engine_pickup":2,"loop_entry":8,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":7,"request_announcements":19,"query_setup":0,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":8,"me